    "visibility" "2"
    "title" "Decoration Blocks"
    "description" "[h1]Decoration Blocks[/h1]
A platform is all machines and belts. This is the other half: 21 textured voxel blocks you can place on the machine layer for no reason except that it looks like somewhere.

Stone, cobblestone, stone bricks, bricks, oak planks and logs, dirt, grass, sand, gravel, snow, glass, bookshelves, obsidian, neitherrack, and solid blocks of gold, iron, diamond, emerald, lapis lazuli and sparkstone.

One block fills exactly one building layer, so they sit on the same grid as everything else and stack three high. Placement is in area mode, so a wall is dragged out as a rectangle rather than clicked one tile at a time.

[h2]Sparkstone[/h2]
A second tab, running a real signal simulation on a 0.1 second tick.

[list]
[*][b]Sparkstone Dust[/b] - carries a strength of 0 to 15 and loses one per tile
[*][b]Torches[/b] - a power source standing free, an inverter mounted on the side of a block
[*][b]Levers and Buttons[/b] - the switches you wire everything else to
[*][b]Repeaters[/b] - refresh a signal to full strength, delay it 1 to 4 ticks, and lock from the side
[*][b]Comparators[/b] - compare or subtract, with inputs from either side and the back
[*][b]Observers[/b] - pulse out of the back whenever the tile they face changes
[*][b]Lamps[/b] - light while powered
[*][b]Block of Sparkstone[/b] - always on
[*][b]Sparkstone Converter[/b] - bridges to shapez wires, both directions at once
[/list]

The converter is the piece that makes this more than decoration. A wire signal that is not Off broadcasts full-strength sparkstone, and sparkstone power puts a true back on the wire - so a lever can gate a belt, and a shape sensor can light a lamp.

Levers, buttons, repeaters and comparators are worked from the side panel: select one and its switch is there. shapez has no click-a-building-in-the-world interaction, so that is where the controls live.

[h2]Before you install[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]This mod affects save games.[/b] Once you install it to a save, you cannot play that save without it.
[*]Requires Shapez Shifter.
[*]Everything is behind a single cheap research node.
[*]Signal state does not survive a save and reload - circuits settle again within a tick or two of loading.
[/list]

Bugs and requests: https://github.com/QuinnBast/Shapez2-Mods/issues
Licensed under Apache 2.0. Block textures are the property of Mojang Studios and are not covered by that license."
    "changenote" "First release."
}
